  "known_limitations": [
    "Tier C (human critical-illness evidence without direct mortality) is currently EMPTY (0 features) -- the LLM extraction rarely emitted the specific exclusion_flags (severity_only/infection_acquisition_only/etc.) needed to distinguish Tier C from Tier D; most non-direct-mortality papers were instead flagged with mechanistic-only reasons (animal/cell/non-ICU). As a result, 'literature_extended' == 'literature_core' (69 features each) at this freeze -- Extended adds nothing new yet. This is reported transparently rather than silently forcing a Tier C bucket.",
    "No 'genome_resolved' (MAG/virulence/BGC) feature rows were extracted by lit04 at all -- despite lit01's view_genome_resolved search queries surfacing 159 candidate PMIDs, the LLM extraction step classified their reportable findings under other feature_view categories or found nothing passage-verifiable. Consequently VFDB_mapping and antiSMASH_mapping are UNMAPPABLE for every feature in this freeze. This mirrors the earlier ad-hoc finding (scripts 34/35, 2026-08-13) that literature directly tying MAG-level resistome/virulence/BGC findings to ICU mortality is sparse.",
    "Cohort duplicate detection (sec. 13) is a coarse heuristic (country+N_total+population+ICU_type exact match) -- it is a conservative flag for manual review, not a validated declaration of shared cohorts.",
    "52 feature-evidence rows had an evidence_passage that did not verify against the source text and were excluded from tier computation; they remain visible in manual_review_queue.csv."
  ],
